      "writtenOn": "2025-11-14T06:25:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the private op is called by our recovery driver. However, we rely on mdcache (stackable FSAL) so that recovery and normal request paths share the same obj_hdl. Recovery sets flags on that handle to block client access while the object may be inconsistent.\nfsal_private_op provides a generic entry point that lets the recovery code invoke our FSAL logic through the same stacked FSAL layers.",
      "parentUuid": "dc91669d_b8fd6c05",
      "revId": "c9923f15805b25dafc72fd073941f722140e4345",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
